---
description: >
  Minimal bug-fix workflow for this project—tight scope, no unrelated refactors, reason from
  code, fix at the right layer, and summarize root cause briefly in Vietnamese. Apply when
  debugging, fixing regressions, or doing targeted fixes; users can also @-mention this rule.
alwaysApply: false
---

# 🎯 TASK

Fix bug in the specified file.

---

# ⚠️ CONTEXT CONTROL (IMPORTANT)

Ignore all previous messages.

Only focus on:
@<file> (limit lines if possible, e.g. 1–200)

---

# 🐛 BUG

<describe clearly>

---

# 🎯 SCOPE

* Minimal change only
* Do NOT refactor unrelated code
* Do NOT change architecture
* Do NOT touch other files unless absolutely required

---

# 🔒 CONSTRAINTS

* Keep existing behavior intact
* No side effects
* No new abstraction unless necessary
* Prefer simplest fix

---

# 🧠 DEBUG STRATEGY

1. Identify root cause
2. Fix at the correct layer (UI / Service / Query)
3. Avoid workaround hacks

---

# 🎯 OUTPUT

1. Fixed code (only affected part or file)
2. Root cause (ngắn gọn, tiếng Việt)
3. Why this fix is correct

---

# 🚫 STRICT RULES

* No over-engineering
* No guessing → must reason from code
* No large refactor

---

# 🎯 GOAL

* Fix đúng bug
* Không phát sinh bug mới
* Code clean, minimal, maintainable
